                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ff19a6b3-99c3-399e-9aa1-2e8cd9f00234",
                        "entry_id": "2545b46f-29c1-38ff-926e-c384878d56c5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Making or implying a promise; promising."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "34a1db47-3991-431b-ba41-cd65650ee10e",
                                "sense_id": "ff19a6b3-99c3-399e-9aa1-2e8cd9f00234",
                                "text": "I answer, that the word may be considered under a double notion, either as it is operative of faith, or as it is promissive of rest to believers: take it as operative of faith, and so it profits, not being mixed with faith, otherwise faith could not come by hearing, as the apostle asserts, (Rom. x. 17); but take it as promissive of rest to believers, and so it doth not profit, not being mixed with faith; that is, faith, which is the condition of the promise, not being performed, the eternal rest, which is the thing promised, cannot belong to them: and this is clearly the apostle's meaning;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d089603-663b-452b-8045-06304af3cea2",
                                "sense_id": "ff19a6b3-99c3-399e-9aa1-2e8cd9f00234",
                                "text": "The performing of the promises cancelled the promissive words; for if they were yet promissive, then what was promised is not performed; this was promised by certain signs. Those promissive signs are cancelled, because the promissive Verity is exhibited."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c1479609-d5bf-43b3-8968-fca1ad324a82",
                                "sense_id": "ff19a6b3-99c3-399e-9aa1-2e8cd9f00234",
                                "text": "The group of substnces which binds and effects the physiology of the biomembrane is promissive in relation with its effect against cancer, on immune system, cell differentiation and aging."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "97a66056-f5d8-361c-8d2c-b876051fd102",
                        "entry_id": "2545b46f-29c1-38ff-926e-c384878d56c5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Implying that the speaker intends to do something or guarantees something."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "716e80f0-b98e-4052-b08e-9d9318964343",
                                "sense_id": "97a66056-f5d8-361c-8d2c-b876051fd102",
                                "text": "Changing the expression—shall is predictive, and will is promissive in the first person only; whereas, in the second and third, will is predictive, and shall promissive."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "259627dc-c39a-4b56-b3d4-832e51b4df13",
                                "sense_id": "97a66056-f5d8-361c-8d2c-b876051fd102",
                                "text": "As we will see, Korean also has promissive and propositive speech act sentence particles, which encode commitment and suggestion, respectively, and exclamative/mirative, indicating a surprise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "168484f2-09e8-4b7e-b916-840d64078ae0",
                                "sense_id": "97a66056-f5d8-361c-8d2c-b876051fd102",
                                "text": "Shall is simply predictive; will is predictive and promissive as well."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
